
days = int(input("Enter required validity days: "))
budget = int(input("Enter your budget: "))

plans = [
    ["Plan A", 199, 2, 28],
    ["Plan B", 299, 3, 56],
    ["Plan C", 399, 5, 84]
]

best_cost = 99999
best_plan = "No eligible plan"

for plan in plans:
    name = plan[0]
    price = plan[1]
    data = plan[2]
    validity = plan[3]

    if validity >= days and price <= budget:
        if price < best_cost:
            best_cost = price
            best_plan = name

print("Best Plan:", best_plan)

if best_plan != "No eligible plan":
    print("Plan Cost: Rs.", best_cost)
else:
    print("No plan satisfies the conditions.")
Algorithm
1. Start.
2. Read required validity days and budget.
3. Store mobile plan details in a list.
4. Set the minimum cost to a large value.
5. Check each plan's validity and price.
6. If both conditions are satisfied, compare its price with the minimum cost.
7. Select the cheapest eligible plan.
8. Display the selected plan and cost.
9. Stop.
10. Example / Sample Output
Enter required validity days: 50
Enter your budget: 350
Best Plan: Plan B
Plan Cost: Rs. 299

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A([START]) --> B[/Enter usage, required validity and budget/]
    B --> C[/Enter mobile plan details/]
    C --> D[Calculate cost of each plan]
    D --> E[Calculate excess charges]
    E --> F{Plan meets usage, validity and budget?}
    F -->|Yes| G[Select eligible plan]
    F -->|No| H[Check next plan]
    H --> I{More plans available?}
    I -->|Yes| D
    I -->|No| J{Any eligible plan?}
    G --> K[Compare eligible plan costs]
    K --> L[Select lowest cost plan]
    L --> M[/Display best plan and total cost/]
    J -->|No| N[/Display No Eligible Plan/]
    J -->|Yes| K
    M --> O([STOP])
    N --> O
```



